---
import ZerotoAILayout from '../layouts/ZerotoAILayout.astro';
---
<ZerotoAILayout title="Project Pitch">

<section id="anatomy-of-an-agent-the-loop" class="slide level2">
	<h2>Anatomy of an Agent — The Loop</h2>
	<p><strong>An agent is a loop: a model observes state, picks a tool, the harness runs it, the result feeds back — until the task is done.</strong></p>
	<div class="columns">
	<div class="column" style="width:65%;">
	<p><img data-src="https://haas-ai-classes.vercel.app/diagrams/c4-recurring-loop.png" style="width:100.0%"></p>
	</div><div class="column" style="width:35%;">
	<p><img data-src="https://haas-ai-classes.vercel.app/diagrams/anakin-padme-ai-agent.png" style="width:100.0%"></p>
	</div></div>
	<div class="fragment">
	<p>Every real agent framework — Claude Code, LangGraph, OpenAI Agents SDK, a hand-rolled Python <code>while</code> loop — wraps the <strong>same four parts</strong> into that loop. The only thing that changes is <strong>how much of the harness you write yourself.</strong></p>
	</div>
</section>

</ZerotoAILayout>

